    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and rewired everything that keys off the household, all in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the `Owner` model already exposed the needed accessors).\n\n**`householdId(lastName, postcode)`** \u2014 now returns the first 12 hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)` (normalized last name = trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, lower-cased), dropping the old `HH-` prefix and the address-based key.\n\n**`addOwner` flow** now:\n1. Computes and assigns the `householdId` **up front**, right after postcode validation \u2014 so every owner gets one deterministically from `(lastName, postcode)`.\n2. Runs the hard-duplicate check on the full `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`), which now carries the real household segment \u2014 so an exact repeat still 409s even with `sharesHousehold` (Cp28).\n3. Adds a **household-duplicate check**: if any existing owner shares the computed `householdId`, reject with 409 **unless** `sharesHousehold` is set (Cp10 / Cp35). `sharesHousehold` now only bypasses this block; it no longer creates the link.\n4. Sets `householdSize` from the computed household membership (`members + 1`).\n5. Skips the possible-duplicate soft-match for declared members, so a declared household member is created and **not** flagged as a suspected duplicate (`possibleDuplicate=false`, Cp35).\n\n**`findHouseholdMembers`** now takes the computed `householdId` and returns existing owners sharing it, instead of matching on last name + address.\n\nResult: `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS, 50 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including all the household checkpoints (Cp03, Cp10, Cp11, Cp13, Cp23, Cp25, Cp28, Cp35, Cp36).",
